# Independent review: local Pages journal storage

Verdict: no remaining blocking finding in the reviewed local storage scope.
Reviewed the chapter 15 append-only journal contract, AGENTS.md, model/store/public exports, module README, and six real-Git tests. Final source snapshots under source/ identify the exact reviewed bytes (57ad064 plus the shallow-repository fix); this review does not presume later commits have identical contents.

Two independently reproduced findings were corrected by the implementation owner:

- A valid current tree could rewrite an old event/evidence pair on a fast-forward descendant, and both load and append accepted it. rewrite-repro.json preserves the original successful counterexample. Final history validation checks a complete single-parent chain and each original pair's added blob identities. rewrite-final.json now records rejection by both operations and an unchanged ref.
- Git shallow boundaries hid an invalid same-tree parent commit from history traversal. shallow-repro.json preserves that successful counterexample. The repository boundary now explicitly rejects shallow repositories; shallow-final.json confirms rejection. Git replacement objects are also disabled in the subprocess command.

Independent execution: six repository tests passed normally and with Python -O. These cover exact evidence retention/reload, sole parent and stale expected head, two real concurrent writers with one CAS winner, invalid typed/event/JSON/size/count inputs, non-bare preservation, historical rewrite rejection and shallow-parent rejection. commands.json and raw stdout/stderr preserve exit codes and output. The independent rewrite and shallow probes also pass after the fixes.

Code review confirms exact envelope fields and canonical bytes, strict integer identities, consecutive records, digest comparison over original evidence bytes, regular blobs, configured size/event/total limits, previous blob retention and old-head Git update-ref CAS. The full maximum-sized journal and every numeric boundary were not independently exercised; inspection is not reported as execution.

The README correctly limits this to local bare-Git storage. Event-specific evidence interpretation, publisher/recovery state transitions, remote fast-forward push and protected-ref confirmation, API reconciliation, live Pages smoke, LKG promotion and deployment authorization remain outside this implementation. Local CAS does not establish any of those. No network/deployment or complete publisher acceptance was performed by this reviewer. Production implementation was not edited.
